        {
          "_type": "UMLPackage",
          "_id": "c4-pkg-0140",
          "_parent": {
            "$ref": "c4-model-0002"
          },
          "name": "2 — Containers",
          "documentation": "Inside the pipeline. Every stage is a separately-invoked Node CLI, so the stages do not call each other — they hand work over through out/. The numbers are the order you run them in; there are deliberately no arrows between stages, because there are no calls between stages.",
          "ownedElements": [
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0141",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0140"
              },
              "name": "0 · Author",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: author.mjs · Node.js\n\nTurns an observed walk of the app into the DSL. Reads a trace — the selectors found and the wait times measured — and emits the .demo and its selector sidecar together. Sizes the narration to each measured wait, reports any line that will not fit, and proposes a SPEEDS_MS range for whatever narration cannot cover. Optional: a .demo can be written by hand."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0142",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0140"
              },
              "name": "1 · Script Compiler",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: script.mjs · Node.js\n\nCompiles a .demo flow into a normal, inspectable scenario module. Refuses to clobber a hand-written scenario. driver.mjs also calls it on the way in."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0143",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0140"
              },
              "name": "2 · Driver",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: driver.mjs · Node.js + puppeteer-core\n\nLaunches Chrome, signs in if the target says to, runs the flow, and records a screencast plus cursor, click and narration-cue telemetry. Closes Chrome cleanly so cookies flush."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0144",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0140"
              },
              "name": "3 · Assembler",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: assemble.mjs · Node.js + ffmpeg\n\nTurns frames into raw.mp4 / cut.mp4. Applies CUTS_MS (drop) and SPEEDS_MS (keep, play fast) and puts the cursor and narration telemetry through the same shift, so nothing desyncs. Prints the largest inter-frame gaps."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0145",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0140"
              },
              "name": "4 · Zoom Projector",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: project.mjs · Node.js\n\nClusters clicks less than 2.5s apart into zoom regions, each carrying a focusTrack the compositor pans across, and writes demo.recordly."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0146",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0140"
              },
              "name": "5 · Compositor",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: compose.mjs · Node.js + canvas + ffmpeg\n\nRenders every frame: eased zoom/pan, a synthesized cursor with click ripples, and a styled window frame. Frames stream through ffmpeg both ways; nothing hits disk."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0147",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0140"
              },
              "name": "6 · Narrator",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: narrate.mjs · Node.js + ffmpeg\n\nVoices the say-cues, trims the breath off each clip, levels every clip to a common loudness, and mixes them onto the video. Extends the video by holding the last frame if a closing line overruns it."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0148",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0140"
              },
              "name": "7 · Tightener",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: tighten.mjs · Node.js + ffmpeg\n\nCompresses stretches that are frozen AND silent, trims the trailing run, and crossfades every seam. Runs after narrate because silence is only meaningful once the voice is on the timeline. Refuses to write if a seam lands on speech or a zoom."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0149",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0140"
              },
              "name": "8 · Card Renderer",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: cards.mjs · Node.js + canvas + ffmpeg\n\nRenders branded intro/outro title cards, voices them with the same provider, and dissolves them on with the concat filter rather than the demuxer."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0150",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0140"
              },
              "name": "Flow definitions",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0008"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: input/ + scenarios/ authored, scripts/ generated\n\nWhat happens on screen and what is said over it. Split by who writes it: input/ holds the plain-English .flow and scenarios/ the .trace.json observed from walking it, both authored and worth reviewing; scripts/ holds the .demo the trace generates, plus its selector sidecar, either of which can be deleted and rebuilt. Committed; contains no credentials."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0151",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0140"
              },
              "name": "Targets & secrets",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0008"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: targets/*.json, *.local.json, .env\n\nWhich deployment, and how to sign in. The .json is committed and holds no secrets; the .local.json and .env are gitignored. Any value may be written env:VAR_NAME and is read from the environment at load time."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0152",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0140"
              },
              "name": "Observed traces",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0008"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: scenarios/*.trace.json\n\nWhat the app actually did on a real walk: the selector each step needs, the evidence for it, and how long every wait took. Authored, not generated — it is the only artifact here that cannot be rebuilt from something else, which is why it lives in scenarios/ rather than the gitignored out/. Also carries hazards the DSL cannot yet express, which the author writes into the script header."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0153",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0140"
              },
              "name": "Selector resolutions",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0008"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: scripts/*.selectors.json\n\nWhat each ask description resolved to against the live DOM, plus the evidence for it. Kept beside the script rather than inside it, so the .demo keeps saying what you meant while the machine-found selector stays reviewable on its own. Keyed by intent text, so renaming a selector or reordering the block does not orphan a resolution."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0154",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0140"
              },
              "name": "Brand assets",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0008"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: brand/\n\nStyleGuide.txt (colour and type, the source of truth), the logo, and the font files. One directory is the brand; there is no flag to point elsewhere."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0155",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0140"
              },
              "name": "Work directory",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0008"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: out/\n\nframes/, frames.json, actions.json, the per-take cursor.json and narration.json, demo.recordly, and the MP4 at each stage: raw, cut, final, final-narrated, -tight, -carded. The hand-off between every stage."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0156",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0140"
              },
              "name": "TTS clip cache",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0008"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: out/tts/ · mp3\n\nOne mp3 per line, keyed by provider+voice+text, plus the derived .lead.mp3 with the opening breath trimmed. Re-cutting or re-composing re-bills nothing; only changed lines re-render."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClassDiagram",
              "_id": "c4-dgm-0157",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0140"
              },
